# The reader lays the next conversation out unseen and keeps the shown one meanwhile, but at most
# 150 ms (reader::LEFT_SHOWN): then the next shows as far as it is laid out. That holds when the
# selection moves on (j, a click, Previous/Next; the owner's decision, 2026-10-19) as when the
# shown message leaves the list (a deleted message stayed in the reader for a second or two on a
# slower machine, 2026-10-12). Here the next layout can't finish (hold-reader-layout, as on a
# slow machine), so without the rule the shown message would stay the full 3 s
# (READY_TIMEOUT). Every message is fictional. Run:
#   tools/headless.sh 36 target/debug/sealwax --self-test tests/selftest/reader-leave.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
resize 1440 900
engine-attach
triage-mark-read-on-open false
mail-account Files
files-add newsletter simple dark-promo
assert-list-count 3

# Moving on with j: the newsletter is off the reader well within the 3 s a layout may take.
list-select 0
wait-until assert-files message newsletter
focus list
hold-reader-layout true
measure-leave j 1 1000
assert-files message simple
hold-reader-layout false
wait-until assert-reader-selected

# Deleting: the deleted message is off the reader as quickly.
hold-reader-layout true
measure-leave numbersign 1 1000
assert-list-count 2
hold-reader-layout false
wait-until assert-reader-selected
